Updates the main Express.js server implementation to align with the standard backend template format while preserving all existing functionality.

## Changes Made

- **Updated GET "/" response**: Changed from "Arcanos backend is running 🚀" to "Arcanos backend running"
- **Updated console log**: Changed from "🌐 Server running on port 8080" to "✅ Server running on port ${port}"
- **Improved keep-alive mechanism**: Replaced `setInterval()` with `process.stdin.resume()` for preventing premature exit

## Before/After Comparison

**Before:**
```javascript
app.get('/', (_req, res) => {
  res.send('Arcanos backend is running 🚀');
});

const server = app.listen(port, '0.0.0.0', () => {
  console.log(`🌐 Server running on port ${port}`);
});

setInterval(() => {
  // keep event loop busy, no-op
}, 60_000);
```

**After:**
```javascript
app.get('/', (_req, res) => {
  res.send('Arcanos backend running');
});

const server = app.listen(port, '0.0.0.0', () => {
  console.log(`✅ Server running on port ${port}`);
});

process.stdin.resume();
```

